IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `epd-nouns`
IMPORT `epd-art01-03`
IMPORT `epd-art04`
IMPORT `epd-art05-06`
IMPORT `epd-art07-08`
IMPORT `epd-art09-11`
IMPORT `epd-art12`
IMPORT `epd-art13`
IMPORT `epd-art14-21`

-- The ePrivacy Directive (Directive 2002/58/EC), Publications Office consolidated version of 19.12.2009 -- THE SEAT LAYER OF THE PROVIDER.
--
-- SEAT: the provider of a publicly available electronic communications service, and where Article 4(1) says so the provider of the
-- public communications network: one provider, one service, one subscriber, one event at a time.
--
-- This layer phrases the layer-1 modules (epd-art01-03 ... epd-art14-21) as the questions the provider asks about its own duties and
-- permissions. It restates no rule: every question calls one layer-1 function with every argument named, from plain inputs worded as
-- the provider is asked. The individual's seat (epd-seat.l4) and the sender's seat (epd-seat-sender.l4) are separate layers over the
-- same modules, so the three seats cannot disagree about the law. There is no seat for an authority or a court: their powers appear
-- only as what they mean for the provider ("Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to require me to ...?").
--
-- A DIRECTIVE BINDS MEMBER STATES, NOT PEOPLE. Where the text says "the provider must", the answer says what the Directive puts on the
-- provider as the Directive states it; where it says "Member States shall ensure", the answer says what the Directive requires of the
-- national law. Neither says what any one Member State's transposing law says, or whether a provision has direct effect (NOTES.md).
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER. JUST TRUE = the text says yes. JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words. NOTHING = the text does not
-- answer (silent, self-limited, list not closed, or pointing outside the sources). NOTHING is not "no" (NOTES.md, "Reading a result:
-- FALSE and NOTHING").
--
-- Two kinds of question appear for a duty: "Must I ...?" (does the duty bind on these facts?) and "Have I ...?" (is it met?).
-- "Without undue delay" and similar open phrases are judgments the provider states as a yes/no fact; the text gives no number.

§ `ePrivacy Directive -- the provider's questions`

§§ `Is the Directive on me? (Articles 2 and 3)`

@export Does the Directive apply to the processing I carry out (Art 3)?
GIVEN `I process personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you process personal data?
      `it is in connection with a publicly available electronic communications service I provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in connection with the provision of a publicly available electronic communications service?
      `my network is a public communications network` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the network a public communications network (including one supporting data collection and identification devices)?
      `my network is in the Community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the network in the Community (the European Union)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Directive apply to the processing I carry out` IS
    `Art 3 the Directive applies to the processing` WITH
        `the processing is of personal data` IS `I process personal data`
        `the processing is in connection with the provision of a publicly available electronic communications service` IS `it is in connection with a publicly available electronic communications service I provide`
        `the network is a public communications network, including a public communications network supporting data collection and identification devices` IS `my network is a public communications network`
        `the network is in the Community` IS `my network is in the Community`

@export Is my service a "value added service" (Art 2(g))?
GIVEN `my service needs more traffic data than conveying and billing need` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the service require the processing of traffic data beyond what is necessary for transmitting a communication or billing it?
      `my service needs more location data than conveying and billing need` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the service require the processing of location data other than traffic data beyond what is necessary for transmitting a communication or billing it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my service a value added service` IS
    `Art 2(g) the service is a value added service` WITH
        `the service requires the processing of traffic data beyond what is necessary for the transmission of a communication or the billing thereof` IS `my service needs more traffic data than conveying and billing need`
        `the service requires the processing of location data other than traffic data beyond what is necessary for the transmission of a communication or the billing thereof` IS `my service needs more location data than conveying and billing need`

§§ `Security and breaches (Article 4)`
-- Only for a provider that has a particular risk to its network, or a personal data breach, to deal with.

@export Have I taken the security measures Art 4(1) requires?
GIVEN `I have taken appropriate technical and organisational measures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you taken appropriate technical and organisational measures to safeguard the security of your services?
      `I need to act together with the network provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is acting in conjunction with the provider of the public communications network necessary for network security?
      `I have acted together with the network provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you acted in conjunction with the provider of the public communications network?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I taken the security measures Article 4(1) requires` IS
    `Art 4(1) first sentence the provider's duty to take appropriate measures is met` WITH
        `the provider has taken appropriate technical and organisational measures to safeguard the security of its services` IS `I have taken appropriate technical and organisational measures`
        `acting in conjunction with the provider of the public communications network is necessary with respect to network security` IS `I need to act together with the network provider`
        `the provider has acted in conjunction with the provider of the public communications network` IS `I have acted together with the network provider`

@export Do my measures include at least what Art 4(1a) requires?
GIVEN `my measures limit access to authorised staff for lawful purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your measures ensure that personal data can be accessed only by authorised personnel for legally authorised purposes?
      `my measures protect data against loss, alteration and unauthorised processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your measures protect personal data against accidental or unlawful destruction, loss or alteration, and unauthorised or unlawful storage, processing, access or disclosure?
      `I have a security policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your measures ensure the implementation of a security policy for processing personal data?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my measures include at least what Article 4(1a) requires` IS
    `Art 4(1a) the measures include at least what the three dashes require` WITH
        `the measures ensure that personal data can be accessed only by authorised personnel for legally authorised purposes` IS `my measures limit access to authorised staff for lawful purposes`
        `the measures protect personal data stored or transmitted against accidental or unlawful destruction, accidental loss or alteration, and unauthorised or unlawful storage, processing, access or disclosure` IS `my measures protect data against loss, alteration and unauthorised processing`
        `the measures ensure the implementation of a security policy with respect to the processing of personal data` IS `I have a security policy`

@export Must I warn my subscribers of a particular risk to the security of the network (Art 4(2))?
GIVEN `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I warn my subscribers of a particular risk to the security of the network` IS
    `Art 4(2) the provider must inform the subscribers concerning the risk` WITH
        `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` IS `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network`

@export Have I warned my subscribers as Art 4(2) requires?
GIVEN `I told my subscribers of the risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you informed the subscribers of the risk?
      `the risk is outside my own measures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the risk lie outside the scope of the measures you must take?
      `I told them of the remedies and likely costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you informed them of the possible remedies, with an indication of the likely costs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I warned my subscribers as Article 4(2) requires` IS
    `Art 4(2) the provider's duty to inform the subscribers is met` WITH
        `the provider has informed the subscribers concerning the risk` IS `I told my subscribers of the risk`
        `the risk lies outside the scope of the measures to be taken by the service provider` IS `the risk is outside my own measures`
        `the provider has informed the subscribers of any possible remedies, including an indication of the likely costs involved` IS `I told them of the remedies and likely costs`

@export Must I notify the authority of this personal data breach (Art 4(3))?
GIVEN `there has been a personal data breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has there been a personal data breach?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I notify the authority of this personal data breach` IS
    `Art 4(3) first subparagraph the provider must notify the competent national authority` WITH
        `there has been a personal data breach` IS `there has been a personal data breach`

-- The text gives no number of hours: "without undue delay" is the provider's own yes/no judgment.
@export Have I notified the authority in time (Art 4(3))?
GIVEN `I notified the authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you notified the personal data breach to the competent national authority?
      `I did it without undue delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do so without undue delay?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I notified the authority in time` IS
    `Art 4(3) first subparagraph the provider's duty to notify the authority is met` WITH
        `the provider notified the personal data breach to the competent national authority` IS `I notified the authority`
        `the provider did so without undue delay` IS `I did it without undue delay`

@export Must I also notify the subscriber or individual affected (Art 4(3))?
GIVEN `there has been a personal data breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has there been a personal data breach?
      `it is likely to harm the subscriber's or individual's data or privacy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it likely to adversely affect the personal data or privacy of a subscriber or individual?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I also notify the subscriber or individual affected` IS
    `Art 4(3) second subparagraph the provider must also notify the subscriber or individual` WITH
        `there has been a personal data breach` IS `there has been a personal data breach`
        `the personal data breach is likely to adversely affect the personal data or privacy of a subscriber or individual` IS `it is likely to harm the subscriber's or individual's data or privacy`

@export Have I notified the subscriber or individual in time (Art 4(3))?
GIVEN `I notified the subscriber or individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you notified the subscriber or individual of the breach?
      `I did it without undue delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do so without undue delay?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I notified the subscriber or individual in time` IS
    `Art 4(3) second subparagraph the provider's duty to notify the subscriber or individual is met` WITH
        `the provider notified the subscriber or individual of the breach` IS `I notified the subscriber or individual`
        `the provider did so without undue delay` IS `I did it without undue delay`

-- POLARITY SWAP: the layer-1 function asks "is notification to the subscriber or individual required?", and answers JUST FALSE where the text says it is not required (the provider is excused).
-- Here JUST TRUE = yes and JUST FALSE = no; the layer-1 function `Art 4(3) third subparagraph the notification to the subscriber or individual is required` answers the opposite question, so its two definite answers are swapped in this DECIDE. NOTHING is left alone (NOTES.md, "Seat polarity audit").
@export Am I excused from notifying the subscriber because I protected the data (Art 4(3))?
GIVEN `I have shown the authority I had appropriate protection measures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you demonstrated to the competent authority's satisfaction that you implemented appropriate technological protection measures?
      `those measures covered the data in the breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were those measures applied to the data concerned by the breach?
      `they make the data unintelligible to anyone unauthorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the measures render the data unintelligible to any person not authorised to access it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I excused from notifying the subscriber because I protected the data` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (`Art 4(3) third subparagraph the notification to the subscriber or individual is required` WITH `the provider has demonstrated to the satisfaction of the competent authority that it has implemented appropriate technological protection measures` IS `I have shown the authority I had appropriate protection measures`, `those measures were applied to the data concerned by the security breach` IS `those measures covered the data in the breach`, `those measures render the data unintelligible to any person who is not authorised to access it` IS `they make the data unintelligible to anyone unauthorised`) EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`Art 4(3) third subparagraph the notification to the subscriber or individual is required` WITH `the provider has demonstrated to the satisfaction of the competent authority that it has implemented appropriate technological protection measures` IS `I have shown the authority I had appropriate protection measures`, `those measures were applied to the data concerned by the security breach` IS `those measures covered the data in the breach`, `those measures render the data unintelligible to any person who is not authorised to access it` IS `they make the data unintelligible to anyone unauthorised`) EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@export May the authority require me to notify the subscriber or individual (Art 4(3))?
GIVEN `I have not yet notified the subscriber or individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you not already notified the subscriber or individual of the breach?
      `the authority has considered the likely adverse effects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the competent national authority considered the likely adverse effects of the breach?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the authority require me to notify the subscriber or individual` IS
    `Art 4(3) fourth subparagraph the competent national authority may require the provider to notify the subscriber or individual` WITH
        `the provider has not already notified the subscriber or individual of the personal data breach` IS `I have not yet notified the subscriber or individual`
        `the competent national authority has considered the likely adverse effects of the breach` IS `the authority has considered the likely adverse effects`

@export Does my notice to the subscriber say what Art 4(3) requires?
GIVEN `it describes the nature of the breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice describe the nature of the personal data breach?
      `it gives contact points` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the contact points where more information can be obtained?
      `it recommends measures to limit the harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it recommend measures to mitigate the possible adverse effects?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my notice to the subscriber say what Article 4(3) requires` IS
    `Art 4(3) fifth subparagraph the notification to the subscriber or individual has the content required` WITH
        `the notification describes the nature of the personal data breach` IS `it describes the nature of the breach`
        `the notification describes the contact points where more information can be obtained` IS `it gives contact points`
        `the notification recommends measures to mitigate the possible adverse effects of the personal data breach` IS `it recommends measures to limit the harm`

-- "in addition" is read as cumulative: everything the notice to the subscriber must say, and the consequences and the measures (NOTES.md, fork register).
@export Does my notice to the authority say what Art 4(3) requires?
GIVEN `it describes the nature of the breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice describe the nature of the personal data breach?
      `it gives contact points` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the contact points where more information can be obtained?
      `it recommends measures to limit the harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it recommend measures to mitigate the possible adverse effects?
      `it describes the consequences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it describe the consequences of the breach?
      `it describes what I have done or propose to do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it describe the measures you have proposed or taken to address the breach?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my notice to the authority say what Article 4(3) requires` IS
    `Art 4(3) fifth subparagraph the notification to the competent national authority has the content required` WITH
        `the notification describes the nature of the personal data breach` IS `it describes the nature of the breach`
        `the notification describes the contact points where more information can be obtained` IS `it gives contact points`
        `the notification recommends measures to mitigate the possible adverse effects of the personal data breach` IS `it recommends measures to limit the harm`
        `the notification describes the consequences of the personal data breach` IS `it describes the consequences`
        `the notification describes the measures proposed or taken by the provider to address the personal data breach` IS `it describes what I have done or propose to do`

@export May the authority adopt guidelines or give me instructions on how I must notify breaches (Art 4(4))?
GIVEN `it is about when I must notify, the format or the manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the measure concern the circumstances in which providers must notify breaches, the format of the notification or the manner of notifying?
      `it is an instruction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the measure an instruction (rather than a guideline)?
      `the instruction is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instruction necessary?
      `technical implementing measures under paragraph 5 cover the point` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do technical implementing measures adopted under Art 4(5) cover the point?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the authority adopt guidelines or give me instructions on notifying breaches` IS
    `Art 4(4) first subparagraph the competent national authority may adopt the guideline or issue the instruction` WITH
        `the measure concerns the circumstances in which providers are required to notify personal data breaches, the format of the notification or the manner in which it is made` IS `it is about when I must notify, the format or the manner`
        `the measure is an instruction` IS `it is an instruction`
        `the instruction is necessary` IS `the instruction is necessary`
        `technical implementing measures adopted under paragraph 5 cover the point` IS `technical implementing measures under paragraph 5 cover the point`

@export Is my inventory of personal data breaches as Art 4(4) requires?
GIVEN `it records the facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the inventory comprise the facts surrounding the breach?
      `it records the effects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it comprise the effects of the breach?
      `it records the remedial action taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it comprise the remedial action taken?
      `it is enough for the authority to check my compliance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it sufficient to enable the competent national authorities to verify compliance with paragraph 3?
      `it holds only what is needed for that` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include only the information necessary for this purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my inventory of personal data breaches as Article 4(4) requires` IS
    `Art 4(4) second subparagraph the provider's inventory of personal data breaches is as required` WITH
        `the inventory comprises the facts surrounding the breach` IS `it records the facts`
        `the inventory comprises the effects of the breach` IS `it records the effects`
        `the inventory comprises the remedial action taken` IS `it records the remedial action taken`
        `the inventory is sufficient to enable the competent national authorities to verify compliance with paragraph 3` IS `it is enough for the authority to check my compliance`
        `the inventory includes only the information necessary for this purpose` IS `it holds only what is needed for that`

@export Must the authority impose sanctions on me if I failed to notify (Art 4(4))?
GIVEN `I failed to comply with my notification obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with your notification obligations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the authority impose sanctions on me if I failed to notify` IS
    `Art 4(4) first subparagraph the competent national authority must impose appropriate sanctions on the provider` WITH
        `the provider has failed to comply with its notification obligations` IS `I failed to comply with my notification obligations`

§§ `Confidentiality and traffic data (Articles 5 and 6)`

@export Must interception of my customers' communications be prohibited, including by me (Art 5(1))?
GIVEN `it is listening, tapping, storage, interception or surveillance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it listening, tapping, storage or another kind of interception or surveillance?
      `it is of communications or related traffic data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it of communications or the related traffic data?
      `it is by someone other than a user` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it by someone other than a user of the communication?
      `the users concerned consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the users concerned consent?
      `it is legally authorised under Article 15(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it legally authorised in accordance with Article 15(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must interception of my customers' communications be prohibited including by me` IS
    `Art 5(1) second sentence the Directive requires the act to be prohibited` WITH
        `the act is listening, tapping, storage or another kind of interception or surveillance` IS `it is listening, tapping, storage, interception or surveillance`
        `the act is of communications or of the related traffic data` IS `it is of communications or related traffic data`
        `the act is by a person other than a user` IS `it is by someone other than a user`
        `the users concerned have consented` IS `the users concerned consented`
        `the person is legally authorised to do so in accordance with Article 15(1)` IS `it is legally authorised under Article 15(1)`

-- JUST FALSE = the paragraph does not prevent it.
@export Does the confidentiality rule stop me storing data technically needed to carry a communication (Art 5(1))?
GIVEN `the storage is technical and necessary for the conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it technical storage necessary for conveying a communication?
      `it is without prejudice to confidentiality` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it without prejudice to the principle of confidentiality?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the confidentiality rule stop me storing data technically needed to carry a communication` IS
    `Art 5(1) third sentence the paragraph prevents the storage` WITH
        `the storage is technical storage which is necessary for the conveyance of a communication` IS `the storage is technical and necessary for the conveyance`
        `the storage is without prejudice to the principle of confidentiality` IS `it is without prejudice to confidentiality`

-- POLARITY SWAP: the layer-1 function asks "does paragraph 1 affect the recording?", and answers JUST FALSE where the text says it shall not (the recording may go ahead).
-- Here JUST TRUE = yes and JUST FALSE = no; the layer-1 function `Art 5(2) paragraph 1 affects the recording` answers the opposite question, so its two definite answers are swapped in this DECIDE. NOTHING is left alone (NOTES.md, "Seat polarity audit").
@export May I record communications in the course of lawful business to prove a transaction (Art 5(2))?
GIVEN `the recording is legally authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the recording legally authorised?
      `it is of communications and related traffic data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it of communications and the related traffic data?
      `it is in the course of lawful business practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it carried out in the course of lawful business practice?
      `it is to provide evidence of a business transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for the purpose of providing evidence of a commercial transaction or other business communication?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I record communications in the course of lawful business to prove a transaction` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (`Art 5(2) paragraph 1 affects the recording` WITH `the recording is legally authorised` IS `the recording is legally authorised`, `the recording is of communications and the related traffic data` IS `it is of communications and related traffic data`, `the recording is carried out in the course of lawful business practice` IS `it is in the course of lawful business practice`, `the recording is for the purpose of providing evidence of a commercial transaction or of any other business communication` IS `it is to provide evidence of a business transaction`) EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`Art 5(2) paragraph 1 affects the recording` WITH `the recording is legally authorised` IS `the recording is legally authorised`, `the recording is of communications and the related traffic data` IS `it is of communications and related traffic data`, `the recording is carried out in the course of lawful business practice` IS `it is in the course of lawful business practice`, `the recording is for the purpose of providing evidence of a commercial transaction or of any other business communication` IS `it is to provide evidence of a business transaction`) EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@export Do I need consent to store information on, or read it from, a subscriber's device (Art 5(3))?
GIVEN `it is storing or gaining access to information in the terminal equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the storing of information in a subscriber's or user's terminal equipment, or the gaining of access to information already stored there?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I need consent to store information on or read it from a subscribers device` IS
    `Art 5(3) first sentence the storing or access is only allowed on condition of consent` WITH
        `the act is the storing of information, or the gaining of access to information already stored, in the terminal equipment of a subscriber or user` IS `it is storing or gaining access to information in the terminal equipment`

@export Have I met the condition of consent for what I store on, or read from, a device (Art 5(3))?
GIVEN `the subscriber gave consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the subscriber or user give consent?
      `I gave clear and comprehensive information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give clear and comprehensive information, including about the purposes?
      `the consent and information meet Directive 95/46/EC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the consent and information in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met the condition of consent for what I store on or read from a device` IS
    `Art 5(3) first sentence the condition of consent is met` WITH
        `the subscriber or user concerned has given his or her consent` IS `the subscriber gave consent`
        `the subscriber or user was provided with clear and comprehensive information, inter alia about the purposes of the processing` IS `I gave clear and comprehensive information`
        `the consent and the information are in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS `the consent and information meet Directive 95/46/EC`

-- JUST FALSE = the first sentence does not prevent it.
@export Does the consent rule stop storage or access that is strictly necessary for a service the user requested (Art 5(3))?
GIVEN `it is technical storage or access` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it technical storage or access?
      `it is for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication over an electronic communications network?
      `the user explicitly requested the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the subscriber or user explicitly request the service from the provider of the information society service?
      `it is strictly necessary for that service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the storage or access strictly necessary for the provider to give that service?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the consent rule stop storage strictly necessary for a service the user requested` IS
    `Art 5(3) second sentence the first sentence prevents the storage or access` WITH
        `it is technical storage or access` IS `it is technical storage or access`
        `it is for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication over an electronic communications network` IS `it is for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication`
        `the provider of an information society service was explicitly requested by the subscriber or user to provide the service` IS `the user explicitly requested the service`
        `the storage or access is strictly necessary in order for that provider to provide the service` IS `it is strictly necessary for that service`

@export Must I erase this traffic data or make it anonymous (Art 6(1))?
GIVEN `it is traffic data I process and store` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it traffic data relating to subscribers and users that you process and store?
      `I no longer need it to carry the communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it no longer needed for the purpose of the transmission of a communication?
      `another rule applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Art 6(2), (3) or (5), or Article 15(1), apply to the data?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I erase this traffic data or make it anonymous` IS
    `Art 6(1) the provider must erase the traffic data or make it anonymous` WITH
        `the data is traffic data relating to subscribers and users, processed and stored by the provider of a public communications network or publicly available electronic communications service` IS `it is traffic data I process and store`
        `the data is no longer needed for the purpose of the transmission of a communication` IS `I no longer need it to carry the communication`
        `paragraph 2, 3 or 5 of this Article or Article 15(1) applies to the data` IS `another rule applies to it`

@export May I process this traffic data for billing on this date (Art 6(2))?
GIVEN `it is data necessary for billing and interconnection payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the data necessary for subscriber billing and interconnection payments?
      `the date of the processing` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you processing it?
      `the last day the bill can be challenged or payment pursued` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day on which the bill may lawfully be challenged or payment pursued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I process this traffic data for billing on this date` IS
    `Art 6(2) the processing of the traffic data for billing is permissible on the date` WITH
        `the data is necessary for the purposes of subscriber billing and interconnection payments` IS `it is data necessary for billing and interconnection payments`
        `the date of the processing` IS `the date of the processing`
        `the last day of the period during which the bill may lawfully be challenged or payment pursued` IS `the last day the bill can be challenged or payment pursued`

@export May I process traffic data for marketing or value added services (Art 6(3))?
GIVEN `it is for marketing electronic communications services or a value added service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose marketing electronic communications services or providing value added services?
      `the subscriber or user gave prior consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the subscriber or user to whom the data relate given prior consent?
      `I go no further than the services or marketing need` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the processing only to the extent and for the duration necessary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I process traffic data for marketing or value added services` IS
    `Art 6(3) first sentence the provider may process the traffic data` WITH
        `the purpose is marketing electronic communications services or the provision of value added services` IS `it is for marketing electronic communications services or a value added service`
        `the subscriber or user to whom the data relate has given his or her prior consent` IS `the subscriber or user gave prior consent`
        `the processing is to the extent and for the duration necessary for such services or marketing` IS `I go no further than the services or marketing need`

@export Have I told the subscriber or user what Art 6(4) requires about traffic data?
GIVEN `the purpose is marketing or a value added service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose marketing or a value added service (which needs consent)?
      `I told them the types of traffic data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you told them the types of traffic data processed?
      `I told them how long` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you told them the duration of the processing?
      `I told them before obtaining consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you tell them before obtaining their consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I told the subscriber what Article 6(4) requires about traffic data` IS
    `Art 6(4) the provider's duty to inform the subscriber or user is met` WITH
        `the purpose is the one mentioned in paragraph 3 (marketing, or value added services)` IS `the purpose is marketing or a value added service`
        `the provider informed the subscriber or user of the types of traffic data which are processed` IS `I told them the types of traffic data`
        `the provider informed the subscriber or user of the duration of such processing` IS `I told them how long`
        `the provider did so prior to obtaining consent` IS `I told them before obtaining consent`

@export Is my staff's handling of traffic data restricted as Art 6(5) requires?
GIVEN `it is by people under my authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the processing by persons acting under your authority as provider?
      `the activity` IS A `Traffic data activity` @desc What is the handling for? One of: billing, traffic management, customer enquiries, fraud detection, marketing electronic communications services, providing a value added service, another activity.
      `it goes no further than that activity needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it restricted to what is necessary for that activity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my staffs handling of traffic data restricted as Article 6(5) requires` IS
    `Art 6(5) the processing of the traffic data is restricted as required` WITH
        `the processing is by a person acting under the authority of a provider of a public communications network or publicly available electronic communications service` IS `it is by people under my authority`
        `activity` IS `the activity`
        `the processing is restricted to what is necessary for the purposes of such activities` IS `it goes no further than that activity needs`

@export May a competent body be told traffic data to settle a dispute (Art 6(6))?
GIVEN `the body is a competent body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a competent body (for example one that settles interconnection or billing disputes)?
      `it is in conformity with applicable legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in conformity with applicable legislation?
      `it is to settle disputes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it with a view to settling disputes, in particular interconnection or billing disputes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a competent body be told traffic data to settle a dispute` IS
    `Art 6(6) the competent body may be informed of the traffic data` WITH
        `the body is a competent body` IS `the body is a competent body`
        `it is informed of traffic data in conformity with applicable legislation` IS `it is in conformity with applicable legislation`
        `it is informed with a view to settling disputes, in particular interconnection or billing disputes` IS `it is to settle disputes`

§§ `Line identification, location, and call forwarding (Articles 8 to 11)`
-- Only for a provider that offers calling or connected line identification, location services, or call forwarding.

@export Have I given the calling user what Art 8(1) requires?
GIVEN `I offer the calling user the possibility of hiding their number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you offer the calling user the possibility of preventing the presentation of their number?
      `it works call by call` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it on a per-call basis?
      `it is simple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it by a simple means?
      `it is free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it free of charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I given the calling user what Article 8(1) requires` IS
    `Art 8(1) first sentence the service provider's duty to the calling user is met` WITH
        `the provider offers the calling user the possibility of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification` IS `I offer the calling user the possibility of hiding their number`
        `the possibility is on a per-call basis` IS `it works call by call`
        `the possibility uses a simple means` IS `it is simple`
        `the possibility is free of charge` IS `it is free`

@export Have I given the called subscriber what Art 8(2) requires?
GIVEN `I offer the possibility of blocking presentation of callers' numbers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you offer the called subscriber the possibility of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification of incoming calls?
      `it is simple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it by a simple means?
      `the use is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subscriber's use of this function reasonable?
      `it is free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it free of charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I given the called subscriber what Article 8(2) requires` IS
    `Art 8(2) the service provider's duty to the called subscriber is met` WITH
        `the provider offers the called subscriber the possibility of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification of incoming calls` IS `I offer the possibility of blocking presentation of callers' numbers`
        `the possibility uses a simple means` IS `it is simple`
        `the use of this function is reasonable` IS `the use is reasonable`
        `the possibility is free of charge` IS `it is free`

@export Have I given the called subscriber what Art 8(3) requires?
GIVEN `I offer the possibility of rejecting calls from hidden numbers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you offer the called subscriber the possibility of rejecting incoming calls where the caller has prevented presentation of their number?
      `it is simple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it by a simple means?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I given the called subscriber what Article 8(3) requires` IS
    `Art 8(3) the service provider's duty to the called subscriber is met` WITH
        `the provider offers the called subscriber the possibility of rejecting incoming calls where the presentation of the calling line identification has been prevented by the calling user or subscriber` IS `I offer the possibility of rejecting calls from hidden numbers`
        `the possibility uses a simple means` IS `it is simple`

@export Have I given the called subscriber what Art 8(4) requires?
GIVEN `I offer the possibility of hiding the connected line identification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you offer the called subscriber the possibility of preventing the presentation of the connected line identification to the caller?
      `it is simple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it by a simple means?
      `it is free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it free of charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I given the called subscriber what Article 8(4) requires` IS
    `Art 8(4) the service provider's duty to the called subscriber is met` WITH
        `the provider offers the called subscriber the possibility of preventing the presentation of the connected line identification to the calling user` IS `I offer the possibility of hiding the connected line identification`
        `the possibility uses a simple means` IS `it is simple`
        `the possibility is free of charge` IS `it is free`

@export Must I tell the public about line identification and the possibilities (Art 8(6))?
GIVEN `I offer calling or connected line identification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you offer presentation of calling line identification or connected line identification?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I tell the public about line identification and the possibilities` IS
    `Art 8(6) the provider must inform the public of the line identification and of the possibilities` WITH
        `presentation of calling line identification or connected line identification is offered` IS `I offer calling or connected line identification`

@export Have I told the public as Art 8(6) requires?
GIVEN `I tell the public that presentation is offered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you inform the public that presentation is offered?
      `I tell the public of the possibilities in Art 8(1) to (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you inform the public of the possibilities set out in paragraphs 1, 2, 3 and 4?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I told the public as Article 8(6) requires` IS
    `Art 8(6) the provider's duty to inform the public is met` WITH
        `the provider informs the public that presentation is offered` IS `I tell the public that presentation is offered`
        `the provider informs the public of the possibilities set out in paragraphs 1, 2, 3 and 4` IS `I tell the public of the possibilities in Art 8(1) to (4)`

@export May I process location data (other than traffic data)(Art 9(1))?
GIVEN `it is location data of users or subscribers of a public network or service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it location data other than traffic data, relating to users or subscribers of public networks or publicly available services?
      `I have made it anonymous` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made the data anonymous?
      `the users or subscribers consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the users or subscribers consented?
      `I go no further than the value added service needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the processing only to the extent and for the duration necessary for the value added service?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I process location data other than traffic data` IS
    `Art 9(1) first sentence the location data may be processed` WITH
        `the data is location data other than traffic data, relating to users or subscribers of public communications networks or publicly available electronic communications services` IS `it is location data of users or subscribers of a public network or service`
        `the data is made anonymous` IS `I have made it anonymous`
        `the users or subscribers have consented` IS `the users or subscribers consented`
        `the processing is to the extent and for the duration necessary for the provision of a value added service` IS `I go no further than the value added service needs`

@export Have I told users what Art 9(1) requires before asking consent to location processing?
GIVEN `I told them the type of location data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you told the users or subscribers the type of location data to be processed?
      `I told them the purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you told them the purposes?
      `I told them how long` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you told them the duration?
      `I told them whether a third party receives it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you told them whether the data will be passed to a third party for the value added service?
      `I told them before obtaining consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you tell them before obtaining their consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I told users what Article 9(1) requires before asking consent to location processing` IS
    `Art 9(1) second sentence the service provider's duty to inform is met` WITH
        `the provider informed the users or subscribers of the type of location data other than traffic data which will be processed` IS `I told them the type of location data`
        `the provider informed them of the purposes of the processing` IS `I told them the purposes`
        `the provider informed them of the duration of the processing` IS `I told them how long`
        `the provider informed them whether the data will be transmitted to a third party for the purpose of providing the value added service` IS `I told them whether a third party receives it`
        `the provider did so prior to obtaining their consent` IS `I told them before obtaining consent`

@export Do my users have the temporary refusal Art 9(2) requires?
GIVEN `users can temporarily refuse the processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can users or subscribers temporarily refuse the processing of their location data?
      `it is simple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it by a simple means?
      `it is free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it free of charge?
      `it works for each connection or transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can they do it for each connection to the network or each transmission of a communication?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my users have the temporary refusal Article 9(2) requires` IS
    `Art 9(2) the possibility of temporarily refusing the processing is as required` WITH
        `the user or subscriber has the possibility of temporarily refusing the processing of such data` IS `users can temporarily refuse the processing`
        `the possibility uses a simple means` IS `it is simple`
        `the possibility is free of charge` IS `it is free`
        `the possibility is for each connection to the network or for each transmission of a communication` IS `it works for each connection or transmission`

@export Is the handling of location data restricted as Art 9(3) requires?
GIVEN `it is in accordance with Art 9(1) and (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the processing in accordance with paragraphs 1 and 2?
      `it is by people under my authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it by persons acting under the authority of the provider?
      `it is by people under the value added service provider's authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it by persons acting under the authority of the third party providing the value added service?
      `it goes no further than the value added service needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it restricted to what is necessary for providing the value added service?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the handling of location data restricted as Article 9(3) requires` IS
    `Art 9(3) the processing of the location data is restricted as required` WITH
        `the processing is in accordance with paragraphs 1 and 2` IS `it is in accordance with Art 9(1) and (2)`
        `the processing is by a person acting under the authority of the provider of the public communications network or publicly available communications service` IS `it is by people under my authority`
        `the processing is by a person acting under the authority of the third party providing the value added service` IS `it is by people under the value added service provider's authority`
        `the processing is restricted to what is necessary for the purposes of providing the value added service` IS `it goes no further than the value added service needs`

@export May I override a subscriber's hiding of their number to trace malicious calls (Art 10(a))?
GIVEN `it is an override of hiding the calling number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an override of the elimination of the presentation of calling line identification?
      `it is temporary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it on a temporary basis?
      `the subscriber applied for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it upon the application of a subscriber?
      `it is to trace malicious or nuisance calls` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subscriber requesting the tracing of malicious or nuisance calls?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I override a subscribers hiding of their number to trace malicious calls` IS
    `Art 10(a) first sentence the provider may override the elimination of the presentation of calling line identification` WITH
        `the override is of the elimination of the presentation of calling line identification` IS `it is an override of hiding the calling number`
        `the override is on a temporary basis` IS `it is temporary`
        `the override is upon application of a subscriber` IS `the subscriber applied for it`
        `the subscriber requests the tracing of malicious or nuisance calls` IS `it is to trace malicious or nuisance calls`

@export May I override line identification or location consent for an emergency organisation (Art 10(b))?
GIVEN `it overrides hiding the number or the denial of location consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an override of the elimination of line identification, or of the temporary denial or absence of consent for processing location data?
      `it is line by line` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it on a per-line basis?
      `the organisation deals with emergency calls` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the organisation deal with emergency calls?
      `a Member State recognises it as such` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it recognised as such by a Member State?
      `it is to respond to emergency calls` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for the purpose of responding to emergency calls?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I override line identification or location consent for an emergency organisation` IS
    `Art 10(b) the provider may override for the organisation` WITH
        `the override is of the elimination of the presentation of calling line identification, or of the temporary denial or absence of consent for the processing of location data` IS `it overrides hiding the number or the denial of location consent`
        `the override is on a per-line basis` IS `it is line by line`
        `the organisation deals with emergency calls` IS `the organisation deals with emergency calls`
        `the organisation is recognised as such by a Member State` IS `a Member State recognises it as such`
        `the override is for the purpose of responding to emergency calls` IS `it is to respond to emergency calls`

@export Have I given subscribers what Art 11 requires about call forwarding?
GIVEN `subscribers can stop automatic call forwarding by a third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can subscribers stop automatic call forwarding by a third party to their terminal?
      `it is simple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it by a simple means?
      `it is free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it free of charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I given subscribers what Article 11 requires about call forwarding` IS
    `Art 11 the possibility of stopping the automatic call forwarding is as required` WITH
        `the subscriber has the possibility of stopping the automatic call forwarding` IS `subscribers can stop automatic call forwarding by a third party`
        `the possibility uses a simple means` IS `it is simple`
        `the possibility is free of charge` IS `it is free`

§§ `Directories (Article 12)`

@export Have I given subscribers the information Art 12(1) requires before including them in a directory?
GIVEN `I told them the purposes of the directory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you told subscribers the purpose or purposes of the directory?
      `it has search functions in an electronic version` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the directory have search functions embedded in an electronic version?
      `I told them of the further uses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you told them of the further usage possibilities those search functions allow?
      `I told them free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you tell them free of charge?
      `I told them before including them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you tell them before including them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I given subscribers the information Article 12(1) requires before including them` IS
    `Art 12(1) the subscriber's information before inclusion is as required` WITH
        `the subscriber was informed about the purpose or purposes of the directory` IS `I told them the purposes of the directory`
        `the directory has search functions embedded in an electronic version` IS `it has search functions in an electronic version`
        `the subscriber was informed of the further usage possibilities based on those search functions` IS `I told them of the further uses`
        `the information was free of charge` IS `I told them free of charge`
        `the information was given before the subscriber was included in the directory` IS `I told them before including them`

@export Have I given subscribers the opportunity Art 12(2) requires?
GIVEN `I let them decide whether they are included` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give subscribers the opportunity to determine whether their personal data are included?
      `the data is relevant for the directory's purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the data relevant for the purpose of the directory as you determine it?
      `I let them decide which data are included` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give them the opportunity to determine which data are included?
      `I let them verify it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give them the opportunity to verify the data?
      `I let them correct it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give them the opportunity to correct the data?
      `I let them withdraw it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give them the opportunity to withdraw the data?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I given subscribers the opportunity Article 12(2) requires` IS
    `Art 12(2) first sentence the subscriber's opportunity is as required` WITH
        `the subscriber was given the opportunity to determine whether their personal data are included` IS `I let them decide whether they are included`
        `the data is relevant for the purpose of the directory as determined by the provider of the directory` IS `the data is relevant for the directory's purpose`
        `the subscriber was given the opportunity to determine which of the data are included` IS `I let them decide which data are included`
        `the subscriber was given the opportunity to verify the data` IS `I let them verify it`
        `the subscriber was given the opportunity to correct the data` IS `I let them correct it`
        `the subscriber was given the opportunity to withdraw the data` IS `I let them withdraw it`

@export Is not being included in the directory, and checking, correcting or withdrawing data, free for subscribers as Art 12(2) requires?
GIVEN `not being included is free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is not being included free of charge?
      `verifying is free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is verifying free of charge?
      `correcting is free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is correcting free of charge?
      `withdrawing is free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is withdrawing free of charge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is not being in the directory and correcting data free for subscribers as Article 12(2) requires` IS
    `Art 12(2) second sentence the subscriber's non-inclusion, verifying, correcting and withdrawing are free of charge` WITH
        `not being included in the public subscriber directory was free of charge` IS `not being included is free`
        `verifying personal data was free of charge` IS `verifying is free`
        `correcting personal data was free of charge` IS `correcting is free`
        `withdrawing personal data from the directory was free of charge` IS `withdrawing is free`

§§ `Proceedings, penalties and my own duties to the authority (Articles 13, 15 and 15a)`

@export May I bring legal proceedings against a sender breaching the marketing rules (Art 13(6))?
GIVEN `I am adversely affected by the infringement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you adversely affected by an infringement of the national provisions adopted pursuant to Article 13?
      `I have a legitimate interest in stopping it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a legitimate interest in the cessation or prohibition of the infringement?
      `I am an electronic communications service provider protecting my business interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an electronic communications service provider protecting its legitimate business interests?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I bring legal proceedings against a sender breaching the marketing rules` IS
    `Art 13(6) the person may bring legal proceedings in respect of the infringement` WITH
        `the person is adversely affected by an infringement of national provisions adopted pursuant to Article 13` IS `I am adversely affected by the infringement`
        `the person has a legitimate interest in the cessation or prohibition of the infringement` IS `I have a legitimate interest in stopping it`
        `the person is an electronic communications service provider protecting its legitimate business interests` IS `I am an electronic communications service provider protecting my business interests`

@export May the Member State penalise me for negligently contributing to unsolicited-message infringements (Art 13(6))?
GIVEN `I am a provider of electronic communications services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a provider of electronic communications services?
      `I contributed by my negligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you by your negligence contribute to infringements of the national provisions adopted pursuant to Article 13?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Member State penalise me for negligently contributing to unsolicited message infringements` IS
    `Art 13(6) second sentence the Member State may lay down specific rules on penalties for the provider` WITH
        `the person is a provider of electronic communications services` IS `I am a provider of electronic communications services`
        `the provider by its negligence contributes to infringements of national provisions adopted pursuant to Article 13` IS `I contributed by my negligence`

@export Have I set up the internal procedures Art 15(1b) requires for access requests?
GIVEN `I have internal procedures for responding to requests for access to users' data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you established internal procedures for responding to requests for access to users' personal data based on national provisions adopted pursuant to Art 15(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I set up the internal procedures Article 15(1b) requires for access requests` IS
    `Art 15(1b) first sentence the provider's duty to establish internal procedures is met` WITH
        `the provider has established internal procedures for responding to requests for access to users' personal data based on national provisions adopted pursuant to paragraph 1` IS `I have internal procedures for responding to requests for access to users' data`

@export Must I give the authority information about my access-request procedures (Art 15(1b))?
GIVEN `the authority has demanded it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the competent national authority demanded the information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the authority information about my access request procedures` IS
    `Art 15(1b) second sentence the provider must provide the competent national authority with the information` WITH
        `the competent national authority has demanded the information` IS `the authority has demanded it`

@export Have I given the authority the information Art 15(1b) requires?
GIVEN `I provided information about the procedures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you provide information about the procedures?
      `I provided the number of requests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you provide the number of requests received?
      `I provided the legal justification invoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you provide the legal justification invoked?
      `I provided my response` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you provide your response?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I given the authority the information Article 15(1b) requires` IS
    `Art 15(1b) second sentence the provider's duty to provide the information is met` WITH
        `the provider provided information about those procedures` IS `I provided information about the procedures`
        `the provider provided the number of requests received` IS `I provided the number of requests`
        `the provider provided the legal justification invoked` IS `I provided the legal justification invoked`
        `the provider provided its response` IS `I provided my response`

-- JUST TRUE = yes: the Directive requires the Member State to give the body the power to order the cessation. JUST FALSE = no (another national body for which it is not relevant, "where relevant"). NOTHING = the Directive does not answer.
@export Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to order me, as a provider, to stop an infringement (Art 15a(2))?
GIVEN `it is an infringement of the national rules under this Directive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an infringement of the national provisions adopted pursuant to this Directive?
      `the body is the competent national authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the competent national authority?
      `the body is another national body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body another national body?
      `it is relevant for that body to have the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it relevant that the other national body have the power?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to order me as a provider to stop an infringement` IS
    `Art 15a(2) the body must have the power to order the cessation of the infringement` WITH
        `the infringement is one referred to in paragraph 1` IS `it is an infringement of the national rules under this Directive`
        `the body is the competent national authority` IS `the body is the competent national authority`
        `the body is another national body` IS `the body is another national body`
        `it is relevant that the other national body have the power` IS `it is relevant for that body to have the power`

-- JUST TRUE = yes: the Directive requires the Member State to give the body that power. JUST FALSE = no (another national body for which it is not relevant, "where relevant"). NOTHING = the Directive does not answer.
@export Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to require me, as a provider, to give it information when it investigates (Art 15a(3))?
GIVEN `the body is the competent national authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the competent national authority?
      `the body is another national body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body another national body?
      `it is relevant for that body to have the powers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it relevant that the other national body have the powers and resources?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to require me as a provider to give it information when it investigates` IS
    `Art 15a(3) the body must have the investigative powers and resources, including the power to obtain information` WITH
        `the body is the competent national authority` IS `the body is the competent national authority`
        `the body is another national body` IS `the body is another national body`
        `it is relevant that the other national body have the powers and resources` IS `it is relevant for that body to have the powers`

§§ `Which of my duties bind me on these facts? ("Must I ...?")`

@export Must I offer the calling user the possibility of hiding their number call by call (Art 8(1))?
GIVEN `I offer presentation of calling line identification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you offer presentation of calling line identification?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I offer the calling user the possibility of hiding their number call by call` IS
    `Art 8(1) first sentence the service provider must offer the calling user the possibility of preventing the presentation on a per-call basis` WITH
        `presentation of calling line identification is offered` IS `I offer presentation of calling line identification`

@export Must I let the called subscriber stop callers' numbers being shown to them (Art 8(2))?
GIVEN `I offer presentation of calling line identification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you offer presentation of calling line identification?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I let the called subscriber stop callers numbers being shown to them` IS
    `Art 8(2) the service provider must offer the called subscriber the possibility of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification of incoming calls` WITH
        `presentation of calling line identification is offered` IS `I offer presentation of calling line identification`

@export Must I let the called subscriber reject calls from hidden numbers (Art 8(3))?
GIVEN `I offer presentation of calling line identification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you offer presentation of calling line identification?
      `I present it before the call is established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the calling line identification presented before the call is established?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I let the called subscriber reject calls from hidden numbers` IS
    `Art 8(3) the service provider must offer the called subscriber the possibility of rejecting incoming calls whose presentation was prevented` WITH
        `presentation of calling line identification is offered` IS `I offer presentation of calling line identification`
        `the calling line identification is presented prior to the call being established` IS `I present it before the call is established`

@export Must I let the called subscriber hide the connected line identification (Art 8(4))?
GIVEN `I offer presentation of connected line identification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you offer presentation of connected line identification?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I let the called subscriber hide the connected line identification` IS
    `Art 8(4) the service provider must offer the called subscriber the possibility of preventing the presentation of the connected line identification` WITH
        `presentation of connected line identification is offered` IS `I offer presentation of connected line identification`

@export Must I tell the subscriber or user about the traffic data I process (Art 6(4))?
GIVEN `the purpose is billing or interconnection, or marketing or a value added service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose one mentioned in Art 6(2) (billing, interconnection) or Art 6(3) (marketing, value added services)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I tell the subscriber or user about the traffic data I process` IS
    `Art 6(4) the provider must inform the subscriber or user` WITH
        `the purpose is one mentioned in paragraph 2 or paragraph 3` IS `the purpose is billing or interconnection, or marketing or a value added service`

@export Must I also tell my subscribers of possible remedies and likely costs (Art 4(2))?
GIVEN `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network?
      `the risk is outside my own measures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the risk lie outside the scope of the measures you must take?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I also tell my subscribers of possible remedies and likely costs` IS
    `Art 4(2) the provider must inform the subscribers of any possible remedies, including the likely costs` WITH
        `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` IS `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network`
        `the risk lies outside the scope of the measures to be taken by the service provider` IS `the risk is outside my own measures`

@export Must I tell users before asking their consent to location processing (Art 9(1))?
GIVEN `I am asking for their consent to location processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you obtaining the users' or subscribers' consent to the processing of location data other than traffic data?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I tell users before asking their consent to location processing` IS
    `Art 9(1) second sentence the service provider must inform the users or subscribers before obtaining their consent` WITH
        `the provider is obtaining the consent of the users or subscribers to the processing of location data other than traffic data` IS `I am asking for their consent to location processing`

@export Must users keep the possibility of temporarily refusing location processing (Art 9(2))?
GIVEN `consent has been obtained for location processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the users' or subscribers' consent been obtained for the processing of location data other than traffic data?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must users keep the possibility of temporarily refusing location processing` IS
    `Art 9(2) the user or subscriber must continue to have the possibility of temporarily refusing the processing` WITH
        `consent of the users or subscribers has been obtained for the processing of location data other than traffic data` IS `consent has been obtained for location processing`

@export Must I set up internal procedures for access requests (Art 15(1b))?
GIVEN `I am a provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a provider (of a publicly available electronic communications service or network)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I set up internal procedures for access requests` IS
    `Art 15(1b) first sentence the provider must establish internal procedures for responding to requests for access` WITH
        `the person is a provider` IS `I am a provider`

@export May my Member State require me to keep data for a limited period for the State's purposes (Art 15(1))?
GIVEN `it is a law requiring retention of data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a legislative measure providing for the retention of data?
      `the retention is for a limited period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the retention for a limited period?
      `it is justified on the grounds in Art 15(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it justified on the grounds laid down in paragraph 1 (national security, defence, public security, crime)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my Member State require me to keep data for a limited period` IS
    `Art 15(1) second sentence the Member State may adopt the legislative measure providing for the retention of data` WITH
        `the measure is a legislative measure providing for the retention of data` IS `it is a law requiring retention of data`
        `the retention is for a limited period` IS `the retention is for a limited period`
        `the retention is justified on the grounds laid down in paragraph 1` IS `it is justified on the grounds in Art 15(1)`

@export May my Member State require additional consent for my directory's other purposes (Art 12(3))?
GIVEN `the purpose is other than searching contact details by name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose of the public directory other than the search of contact details of persons on the basis of their name and, where necessary, a minimum of other identifiers?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my Member State require additional consent for my directorys other purposes` IS
    `Art 12(3) the Member State may require additional consent of the subscribers` WITH
        `the purpose of the public directory is other than the search of contact details of persons on the basis of their name and, where necessary, a minimum of other identifiers` IS `the purpose is other than searching contact details by name`

§§ `A few more questions on my duties and the authority's powers (Articles 4, 8 and 10)`

@export Do my security measures ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk (Art 4(1))?
GIVEN `my measures ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk presented, having regard to the state of the art and the cost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your measures ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk presented, having regard to the state of the art and the cost of their implementation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my security measures ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk` IS
    `Art 4(1) second sentence the measures ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk` WITH
        `the measures ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk presented, having regard to the state of the art and the cost of their implementation` IS `my measures ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk presented, having regard to the state of the art and the cost`

@export Have I given the calling subscriber the per-line possibility of hiding their number (Art 8(1))?
GIVEN `the subscriber can prevent the presentation of the calling line identification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the calling subscriber have the possibility of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification?
      `the possibility is on a per-line basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the possibility on a per-line basis?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I given the calling subscriber the per-line possibility of hiding their number` IS
    `Art 8(1) second sentence the calling subscriber's possibility on a per-line basis is met` WITH
        `the calling subscriber has the possibility of preventing the presentation of the calling line identification` IS `the subscriber can prevent the presentation of the calling line identification`
        `the possibility is on a per-line basis` IS `the possibility is on a per-line basis`

@export After I override line identification to trace a malicious call, must I store the data and make it available (Art 10(a))?
GIVEN `I overrode the elimination of calling line identification to trace a malicious call` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you override the elimination of calling line identification under Art 10(a)?
      `the storing is in accordance with national law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the storing and making available in accordance with national law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `After I override line identification to trace a malicious call must I store the data and make it available` IS
    `Art 10(a) second sentence the data identifying the calling subscriber will be stored and made available by the provider` WITH
        `the provider has overridden the elimination of calling line identification under paragraph (a)` IS `I overrode the elimination of calling line identification to trace a malicious call`
        `the storing and making available is in accordance with national law` IS `the storing is in accordance with national law`

@export May a national authority audit my security measures and recommend best practice (Art 4(1a))?
GIVEN `the body is a relevant national authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body that wants to audit your measures a relevant national authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a national authority audit my security measures and recommend best practice` IS
    `Art 4(1a) the national authority can audit the provider's measures and issue recommendations` WITH
        `the body is a relevant national authority` IS `the body is a relevant national authority`

@export May the authority audit whether I complied with my notification duties (Art 4(4))?
GIVEN `the body is a competent national authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body that wants to audit your compliance a competent national authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the authority audit whether I complied with my notification duties` IS
    `Art 4(4) first subparagraph the competent national authority can audit the provider's compliance with its notification obligations` WITH
        `the body is a competent national authority` IS `the body is a competent national authority`
